{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-10-Jul-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A policeman was asked to chase a thief. Before the policeman started the chase, he realised that the thief was 200 metres ahead of him and was running at a speed of 16 km/h. The policeman started the chase at a speed of 20 km/h. How far will the thief run before he is overtaken by the policeman?", "options": [{"text": "1000 m", "added": false}, {"text": "700 m", "added": false}, {"text": "800 m", "added": false}, {"text": "600 m", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "A certain sum of money is lent out at simple interest. If that money becomes ₹24,000 in 2 years and ₹32,000 in 4 years, the annual rate of interest is:", "options": [{"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "16%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "If x ∶ y = 5 ∶ 6,then 2x + 3y ∶ 3x + 5y is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "The ratio of the outer and the inner circumference of a circular path is 7:6. If the path is 45 m wide, then what is the radius (in m) of the inner circle?", "options": [{"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "270", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "After an increase of 9% in salary, a person received ₹6,300. What was his salary before the increase (consider integral part only)?", "options": [{"text": "₹3,879", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,779", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A vendor buys 20 dozen bananas for ₹1,200 and sells 5 dozen for ₹350, then his gain percentage is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "In an isosceles triangle ABC, AB=AC. D is a point inside the triangle such that ∠ BAD = 20° = ∠ DCB, ∠ CAD = 80°. The value of ∠ ABC is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹4.43 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4.7 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4.5 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5.2 lakh", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "A line from point A is drawn that is tangent to the circle at point B. A secant is also drawn from point A to the circle intersecting it at points C and D. If AB = 42 cm and AC = 21 cm, then what is the ratio between AB and CD?", "options": [{"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A cube of edge 4 cm is cut into cubes each of edge of 2 cm. The ratio of the total surface area of one of the small cubes to that of the large cube is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "1 : 64", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 16", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 4", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "108°", "added": false}, {"text": "34°", "added": false}, {"text": "120°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "When 12 is subtracted from a number, it reduces to its 40%. Two-fifth of that number is:", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The length (in cm) of a direct common tangent to two circles of radii 14 cm and 5 cm whose centres are separated by a distance of 40 cm is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1510", "added": false}, {"text": "1360", "added": false}, {"text": "1220", "added": false}, {"text": "1440", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "The curved surface area of a right circular cone is 20π cm2. If its radius is 4 cm, then find the volume of cone.", "options": [{"text": "18 π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "21 π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "20 π cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "16 π cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "In an election there were three candidates. The first candidate got 40% votes and second candidate got 35% votes. If the total votes in the election are 50,000, find the number of votes got by the third candidate.", "options": [{"text": "12000", "added": false}, {"text": "1250", "added": false}, {"text": "12500", "added": false}, {"text": "13,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Ratna buys 10 kg of rice for ₹88 per kg and another 20 kg of rice for ₹187 per kg. What is the per kg cost (in ₹) of the total mixture of rice for her?", "options": [{"text": "148", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "158", "added": false}, {"text": "154", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}]}